# Atomic commits (ActiveSecHarness)

When committing in this repository (`/home/simon/Cursor/ActiveSecHarness`):

- Use **atomic commits**: one logical change per commit.
- Split unrelated changes (e.g. docs vs core vs guard vs wiki vs tests) into separate commits.
- Do not bundle independent features, refactors, or docs updates into a single commit.

This requirement applies only to ActiveSecHarness. Other co-evolving repos (e.g. papermachineclip / LotLImmune) do not require atomic commits.
